  "Laramie asked Carnegie for $50,000, then $40,000, and got $20,000 in 1903; the library by Henry D. Whitfield of New York was dedicated on January 22, 1906. It cost $20,077, and one man paid the $77 over. It was the public library until 1981 and now holds city offices, with an exhibit in the entry and a bronze medallion of Carnegie by the reception desk. On the National Register in 1988.",
