  "Granted $11,000 in 1914 and finished in September 1919, the year Carnegie died, after the Civic Improvement Club raised the money for the lot. Its corner entrance under a CARNEGIE LIBRARY sign is the only one among Wyoming's Carnegie libraries. It shares its block with the 1919 courthouse and the 1914 jail; an east addition came in 1998 and 1999. Built by the local contractor Elmer H. Ranck to Carnegie plans; a 2019 thesis credits the design to William DuBois.",
